title: "perinatal-ews: open-source early-warning analytics for county maternal and newborn health"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tejpal
    given-names: Karan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8609-2854"
version: 0.2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23374647"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23374647"
    description: "Zenodo archive of this software"
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/karantejpal12/perinatal-ews"
abstract: >-
  perinatal-ews scans public natality data and flags counties where maternal and
  newborn outcomes (preterm birth, low birth weight, late or no prenatal care,
  gestational hypertension) are worse than their own recent history and the
  all-county trend predict. It uses empirical-Bayes shrinkage, overdispersion
  modelling and false-discovery-rate control, runs the same test within
  subgroups, reports within-county equity gaps, and monitors its own data
  quality, distribution drift and detection performance.
keywords:
  - public health surveillance
  - maternal health
  - perinatal health
  - natality
  - early warning
  - health equity
  - model monitoring
